; DECISIONS — present-truth ledger (third edition)
; One entry per decision: what holds, why (short), decided-by, date, cite.
; Append or expressly overturn; never silently rewrite. Lower entries
; supersede earlier ones. History and deliberation live in CHANGELOG.md
; and the cited records -- this file stays thin.
;
; decided-by vocabulary (carried forward from the second edition's D1,
; steward-decided there 2026-08-07; re-ratify or amend at will):
;   steward    - steward made the call; agent or council ratified
;   ratified   - agent made the call; steward ratified
;   council    - agent call after red-teaming + unified validation from other agents
;   supported  - agent call with provisional steward/council support; easier revisit
;   defacto    - "decided" without really being decided; recorded so the record exists
;   proposed   - from steward or any agent; not blocking anything yet
;   transition - rejected but still existing somewhere; defacto-but-being-fixed

|decision[decided-by-vocabulary]
  :holds The seven-value decided-by vocabulary above governs this ledger.
  :why The weight of a decision is who stood behind it and how.
  :decided-by steward
  :date <2026-08-08>
  :cite Second edition D1 (in .archive/second-theory-iteration-2026-08-08/DECISIONS.md), carried at reset.

|decision[declared-inflections]
  :holds Each |term is named by its singular (base) form and declares its own
         morphology: :pos (noun, verb, or both, stacked) and, for count nouns,
         :pl (a suffix such as -s or -es, or the whole irregular plural). Tools
         derive every surface form from these declarations; they do not guess.
  :why Writers use a term in whatever form the sentence wants; the term should
       say what its forms are, so links resolve exactly and anything else is
       reported.
  :decided-by steward
  :date <2026-10-09>
  :cite In-session: "Can we just fix the terms a little bit and automatically
        take care of inflections as per however they are used in context?",
        with |term[referent] … :pos noun :pl -s as the example. Applied in
        def/ the same day (referents -> referent).

|decision[regular-verbs-by-rule]
  :holds A term whose :pos includes verb declares nothing more when it is
         regular; the tools conjugate it (3rd person -s/-es, past -ed/-d,
         -ing with a final e dropped). Explicit attributes only for an
         irregular verb.
  :why Extends declared-inflections to verbs without making every entry
       spell out its conjugation.
  :decided-by proposed
  :date <2026-10-09>
  :cite Agent's extension of the steward's noun pattern (Claude, same
        session); awaiting the steward's word.
